Found during the 0.500 pre-release audit (karr-release-checker), item 3 (dist.ini review).

dist.ini has:

    [@Author::GETTY]
    docker_image = raudssus/karr

    [@Author::GETTY::Docker / runtime-root]
    target = runtime-root

    [@Author::GETTY::Docker / runtime-user]
    image = raudssus/karr
    target = runtime-user
    tags = user %V-user %v-user

Per Dist::Zilla::PluginBundle::Author::GETTY (lib/Dist/Zilla/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm:1281-1289 in p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty): whenever docker_image is set AND docker_default is not explicitly 0, the bundle auto-adds one more, unnamed default [@Author::GETTY::Docker] subsection on top of any explicit ones. The bundle's own POD documents this exact case (docker_image + multiple explicit subsections) as needing `docker_default = 0` to "suppress the auto-default; subsections handle it" -- this dist.ini does not set it.

Effect: three Docker::API plugin instances build on every `dzil build`/`dzil release`, not two -- an unnamed default (no target, tags default to "latest %V %v") plus runtime-root (also no explicit tags, so also "latest %V %v") plus runtime-user. The default and runtime-root end up publishing the *same* tags ("latest", "%V", "%v") from what should be two different named build targets -- redundant work, and whichever of the two runs last silently wins the tag.

Not the cause of the current release blocker (that's the CPAN-unreleased Git::Native/Git::Libgit2 pins, tracked separately, not a bug to fix), but worth cleaning up independently: add `docker_default = 0` under [@Author::GETTY] so only the two named subsections build.
